From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:11:02 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - server GUI icon is the SourbyCraft logo

The bundled canvas-logo.png is replaced by sourbycraft-logo.png (from
.github/assets/SourbyCraft.png). The engine's other Canvas-era names
(ticket ids, pearl saved data, JVM flags) are renamed in the engine
baseline, not here.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/gui/MinecraftServerGui.java b/net/minecraft/server/gui/MinecraftServerGui.java
index f4b9f486547569bc208b0163da10ecf3db6124f6..d67f493548309214f7e5b9fce11defe3b265272b 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/gui/MinecraftServerGui.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/gui/MinecraftServerGui.java
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ public class MinecraftServerGui extends JComponent {
         // Paper start - Improve ServerGUI
         frame.setName("Minecraft server");
         try {
-            frame.setIconImage(javax.imageio.ImageIO.read(java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(MinecraftServerGui.class.getClassLoader().getResourceAsStream("canvas-logo.png")))); // Canvas - Use our logo
+            frame.setIconImage(javax.imageio.ImageIO.read(java.util.Objects.requireNonNull(MinecraftServerGui.class.getClassLoader().getResourceAsStream("sourbycraft-logo.png")))); // Canvas - Use our logo // SourbyCraft - the SourbyCraft logo
         } catch (java.io.IOException ignore) {
         }
         // Paper end - Improve ServerGUI
